# Written before the Dockerfile, and .env is the reason.
#
# runner/.env holds the agent's private key. A COPY without this bakes it into
# an image layer, where it survives being deleted by a later layer and travels
# anywhere the image goes. The repo's .gitignore guards a different fence
# around the same field.
.env
.env.*

node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# Scaffolding for local development. The agent's image has no business
# carrying the prompt service it talks to.
dev

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
